---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import ShareButtons from '../../../components/ShareButtons.astro';
import '../../../styles/global.css';
import en from '../../../i18n/en.json';
import { WA_EN } from '../../../data/home-content';

const t = en;
const lang = 'en';

const title = 'Surf School Website Guide: How Canggu Surf Schools Can Take Bookings Directly';
const seoTitle = 'Surf School Website: How Canggu Schools Take Direct Bookings';
const description = 'A surf school website lets Canggu schools take lesson bookings directly instead of paying marketplace commissions: the pages, features, and mistakes to avoid.';
const canonical = 'https://zeepage.com/en/blog/surf-school-website-canggu/';
const cover = '/blog/surf-school-website-canggu.webp';
const coverAlt = 'A surf school website guide for Canggu surf schools taking bookings directly by zeepage';

const structuredData = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BlogPosting',
  headline: title,
  description: description,
  image: 'https://zeepage.com' + cover,
  datePublished: '2026-10-24',
  inLanguage: 'en',
  author: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'zeepage',
    url: 'https://zeepage.com',
  },
  publisher: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'zeepage',
    url: 'https://zeepage.com',
    logo: {
      '@type': 'ImageObject',
      url: 'https://zeepage.com/logo-ui.webp',
    },
  },
  mainEntityOfPage: {
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    '@id': canonical,
  },
};
---

<BaseLayout title={seoTitle + ' | zeepage'} description={description} lang="en" canonical={canonical} structuredData={structuredData} image={'https://zeepage.com' + cover}>
  <Navbar t={t.nav} lang={lang} cta={{ primary: t.hero.cta1, secondary: t.hero.cta2, whatsapp: t.cta.whatsapp, whatsappUrl: t.cta.whatsappUrl }} />
  <main>
    <article>
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pt-32 sm:pt-40">
        <span class="inline-block text-sm font-bold tracking-wide uppercase text-brand bg-accent px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full">Blog</span>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-6xl font-extrabold tracking-tight max-w-4xl mt-6">{title}</h1>
        <p class="text-ink/50 mt-6">October 24, 2026 • by zeepage</p>
        <figure>
          <img src={cover} alt={coverAlt} class="w-full rounded-[2rem] border border-line mt-10" />
        </figure>
    <ShareButtons title={title} url={canonical} lang={lang} extraClass="mt-8" />
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-14">
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">Most surf schools in Canggu sell their lessons the same way: through activity marketplaces, a booking widget borrowed from a platform, or Instagram messages answered one by one. It works, until you count what it costs. Every marketplace booking hands a cut of the lesson price to the platform, the student relationship belongs to the platform, and when a traveler searches Google for surf lessons in Canggu, the results page belongs to the platform too.</p>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">A surf school website of your own changes that balance. It gives your school one address that you control, where lesson prices are yours, the booking lands in your own WhatsApp or inbox, and your school can actually be found by the people planning their Bali trip. This guide walks through what that website needs, page by page, and the mistakes that keep school websites quiet even when they look good.</p>

        <div class="bg-white border border-line rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 mb-12">
    <p class="text-sm font-extrabold uppercase tracking-widest text-ink/40 mb-4">On this page</p>
    <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2.5 text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
      <li><a href="#why-surf-school-website" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">Why a Surf School Website Beats Relying on Marketplaces</a></li>
      <li><a href="#surf-school-website-features" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">What a Surf School Website Needs to Take Bookings Directly</a></li>
      <li><a href="#surf-school-website-pages" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">Surf School Website Pages That Turn Visitors into Students</a></li>
      <li><a href="#surf-camp-website" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">Surf Camp Website or Surf School Website: What Changes</a></li>
      <li><a href="#surf-school-website-mistakes" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">Surf School Website Mistakes That Quietly Cost You Students</a></li>
      <li><a href="#start-surf-school-website-canggu" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">How to Start a Surf School Website in Canggu This Season</a></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <h2 id="why-surf-school-website" class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mt-2 mb-5 scroll-mt-32">Why a Surf School Website Beats Relying on Marketplaces</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">Marketplaces are built to compare you. Your school appears in a list sorted by price and platform ranking, next to every competitor in Canggu, and the traveler is encouraged to keep scrolling. On your own surf school website there is no list. The visitor sees your instructors, your breaks, your prices, and one clear way to book. Schools that look similar on a marketplace suddenly look very different on their own ground.</p>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">There is also the search itself. Many travelers first meet your school on a marketplace, then type your school name into Google to check who you really are. If that search leads to a proper website with lesson details and a booking button, a good share of those students will book direct and save you the commission. If it leads nowhere, they return to the marketplace and the platform keeps both the cut and the customer.</p>

        <h2 id="surf-school-website-features" class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mt-14 mb-5 scroll-mt-32">What a Surf School Website Needs to Take Bookings Directly</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">A surf school website does not need to be complicated. It needs to answer, quickly and honestly, everything a beginner or improving surfer asks before paying for a lesson:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2.5 text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          <li>Lesson types with prices shown openly: group and private lessons, beginner and intermediate levels, kids lessons if you offer them, and multi day packages.</li>
          <li>What is included in the price, such as the board, rash guard, sunscreen, water, and transport to the break, so there are no surprises at the beach.</li>
          <li>How scheduling works with the tides, explained in plain words, since lesson times in Canggu move with the tide chart and first time students rarely know this.</li>
          <li>Instructor profiles with real names, photos, and experience, because students are trusting you with their safety in the ocean.</li>
          <li>A short booking form or a WhatsApp button that opens a chat with the lesson details already filled in.</li>
          <li>The meeting point with a map pin, plus how pickups work for students staying around Berawa, Pererenan, and Batu Bolong.</li>
          <li>A practical FAQ covering what to bring, whether students need to swim well, and what happens when the swell is too big or too small.</li>
          <li>Photos of your real lessons and real students, with their permission, instead of generic surf stock imagery.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="surf-school-website-pages" class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mt-14 mb-5 scroll-mt-32">Surf School Website Pages That Turn Visitors into Students</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">Beyond the features, the page structure matters. A home page that opens with your best lesson photo, your starting price, and a booking button does more than any long introduction. A lessons and pricing page does the comparing for the student, in your favor, by laying out exactly what each level includes. An instructors page builds the trust that makes a nervous beginner commit.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-9 mb-3">A surf spot guide is the hardest working page on a surf school website</h3>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">One page deserves special mention: an honest guide to the breaks you teach at. Explain Batu Bolong for beginners at the right tide, what Echo Beach offers as students progress, and how Berawa changes with the swell. Travelers search for this information while planning, long before they choose a school. The school that answers their questions is the school they book with, and this kind of page keeps bringing visitors from Google month after month.</p>

        <div class="bg-brand text-white rounded-[2rem] p-8 sm:p-10 my-14">
      <h3 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">Still paying commission on every lesson?</h3>
      <p class="text-white/85 leading-relaxed mt-3 mb-7">zeepage builds websites for surf schools in Bali that take bookings directly, starting from just a few hundred thousand rupiah. The consultation is free, tell us how your school runs today.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href={WA_EN} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="bg-white text-brand font-bold rounded-full px-6 py-3">Free Consultation</a>
        <a href="/en/layanan/" class="border border-white/50 text-white font-bold rounded-full px-6 py-3">See Website Services</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <h2 id="surf-camp-website" class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mt-14 mb-5 scroll-mt-32">Surf Camp Website or Surf School Website: What Changes</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">If you run a camp rather than a day school, the website carries more weight, because the guest is buying a week of their holiday, not a two hour lesson. A surf camp website needs everything above, plus room types with rates, what a typical camp week looks like, meals and dietary handling, airport pickup, and package pricing that bundles stay, lessons, and board rental. The booking conversation is longer too, so camps benefit from a proper inquiry form that asks about dates, level, and room preference in one go.</p>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">The principle stays the same for both: the clearer the information, the fewer back and forth messages, and the more bookings arrive already decided. If you operate both a camp and daily lessons, one website can serve both, with the camp packages and the lesson menu as clearly separated sections.</p>

        <h2 id="surf-school-website-mistakes" class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mt-14 mb-5 scroll-mt-32">Surf School Website Mistakes That Quietly Cost You Students</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">Plenty of schools already have a website and still take nearly all bookings through platforms. When we look closely, the reasons tend to repeat:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2.5 text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          <li>No prices anywhere, so visitors leave to compare on a marketplace where prices are visible.</li>
          <li>Booking only through direct messages, with no form or button on the website itself.</li>
          <li>A slow, heavy home page built around background video that struggles on hotel and cafe wifi.</li>
          <li>No explanation of tide based scheduling, leaving beginners confused about why lesson times change daily.</li>
          <li>Contact details that differ between the website and Google Maps, which makes careful travelers hesitate.</li>
          <li>A website that is never mentioned on the school Instagram, at the beach base, or in replies to past students.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="start-surf-school-website-canggu" class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mt-14 mb-5 scroll-mt-32">How to Start a Surf School Website in Canggu This Season</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">Start with the smallest version that can take a booking: a home page with your prices, one lessons page, instructor profiles, and a booking button that reaches you instantly. Connect it to a tidy Google Business Profile with the same name, phone number, and location pin. Then grow it with the surf spot guide and a gallery of real lessons. You can see our packages laid out openly on the <a href="/en/harga/" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">pricing page</a>, and what each service includes on our <a href="/en/layanan/" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">website services page</a>.</p>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">Canggu is one of the most searched surf towns in the world, and its schools compete for students who plan everything online. A clear surf school website is how an independent school stops renting its students from platforms and starts owning the relationship. The sooner it is live, the sooner your name search on Google ends at your own booking button.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pb-20">
        <ShareButtons title={title} url={canonical} lang={lang} extraClass="mt-14" />
    <div class="bg-white border border-line rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 mt-14">
    <p class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">Read next</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2.5 text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
      <li><a href="/en/" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">Web Design Services in Bali: zeepage Home</a></li>
